    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0543" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg449"/>

                <head>No. 300.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Phelps</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 7,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 466.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for your information, a
                    copy of my note<anchor n="‡" xml:id="d300-f1"/> of the 1st instant to Sir Lionel
                    West, Her Britannic Majesty’s minister at this capital, concerning the treatment
                    by the Canadian authorities of the American fishing schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Molly Adams</hi>, of Gloucester, Mass.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. BAYARD.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
